orthant 1 language

- # `↯/s.105.5` — `Certificate.Error`
+ # `↯/s.105.5` — `Certificate.Error`

- Raised when Enigmatic cannot build an X.509 certificate.
+ Se lanza cuando Enigmatic no puede construir un certificado X.509.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Certificate generation refuses inputs that would produce a structurally
- valid certificate that no verifier would accept — a serial number
- outside the range X.509 permits, a validity period that never opens, a
- key whose encoding is not a `SubjectPublicKeyInfo`, or a cipher and
- digest with no object identifier assigned to the pair. The message is
- `could not build the certificate because $reason`.
+ La generación de certificados rechaza las entradas que producirían un certificado
+ estructuralmente válido que ningún verificador aceptaría: un número de serie fuera del rango que
+ permite X.509, un periodo de validez que nunca empieza, una clave cuya codificación no es un
+ `SubjectPublicKeyInfo`, o un cifrado y un resumen sin un identificador de objeto asignado al par.
+ El mensaje es `could not build the certificate because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.105.5.1` — `UnknownAlgorithm`
+ ### `↯/s.105.5.1` — `UnknownAlgorithm`

- The cipher and the ambient `SignatureDigest` have no signature algorithm
- object identifier between them. RSA and ECDSA have identifiers assigned
- for SHA-256, SHA-384 and SHA-512 only.
+ El cifrado y el `SignatureDigest` ambiental no tienen entre ambos un identificador de objeto de
+ algoritmo de firma. RSA y ECDSA tienen identificadores asignados solo para SHA-256, SHA-384 y
+ SHA-512.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.5.1] could not build the certificate because no signature algorithm is assigned to SHA1`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.5.1] could not build the certificate because no signature algorithm is assigned to SHA1`

- **Resolution.** Choose one of the digests that has an identifier; the
- default, SHA-256, is what every current certificate profile mandates.
+ **Solución.** Elige uno de los resúmenes que tienen identificador; el predeterminado, SHA-256, es
+ el que exigen todos los perfiles de certificado actuales.

- ### `↯/s.105.5.2` — `BadPublicKey`
+ ### `↯/s.105.5.2` — `BadPublicKey`

- The key's public half was not a DER `SubjectPublicKeyInfo`, so it cannot
- be embedded in a certificate.
+ La mitad pública de la clave no era un `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` DER, así que no puede incrustarse en
+ un certificado.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.5.2] could not build the certificate because the public key was not a SubjectPublicKeyInfo`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.5.2] could not build the certificate because the public key was not a SubjectPublicKeyInfo`

- **Resolution.** This indicates a provider that does not follow the
- `Crypto` contract's key encodings; check which provider is in scope.
+ **Solución.** Esto indica un proveedor que no sigue las codificaciones de claves del contrato de
+ `Crypto`; comprueba qué proveedor hay en el ámbito.

- ### `↯/s.105.5.3` — `BadSerialNumber`
+ ### `↯/s.105.5.3` — `BadSerialNumber`

- The serial number was zero or negative. RFC 5280 requires a positive
- integer.
+ El número de serie era cero o negativo. La RFC 5280 exige un entero positivo.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.5.3] could not build the certificate because the serial number was negative or zero`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.5.3] could not build the certificate because the serial number was negative or zero`

- **Resolution.** Use a positive serial number; for a certificate
- authority it must also be unique among the certificates it has issued.
+ **Solución.** Usa un número de serie positivo; para una autoridad de certificación, también debe
+ ser único entre los certificados que ha emitido.

- ### `↯/s.105.5.4` — `BadValidity`
+ ### `↯/s.105.5.4` — `BadValidity`

- The validity period's end was not after its start.
+ El final del periodo de validez no era posterior a su inicio.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.105.5.4] could not build the certificate because the validity period ended before it began`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.105.5.4] could not build the certificate because the validity period ended before it began`

- **Resolution.** Build the period with the earlier instant first, as
- `notBefore ~ notAfter`.
+ **Solución.** Construye el periodo con el instante anterior primero, como `notBefore ~ notAfter`.

